# Error Handling Guidelines

## Error Strategy

- Fail fast when encountering invalid states
- Handle errors explicitly rather than silently ignoring them
- Use meaningful error messages that help users understand the issue
- Implement proper error boundaries for React applications

## TypeScript Error Patterns

- Create custom error types for domain-specific errors
- Use Result types or discriminated unions for operations that can fail
- Implement proper null checking and optional chaining
- Use try-catch blocks with typed catch clauses where appropriate

## React Error Handling

- Implement Error Boundaries for component tree protection
- Handle async errors in useEffect with proper cleanup
- Show user-friendly error messages instead of technical details
- Implement proper fallback UI for error states
- Log errors appropriately for debugging

## API Error Handling

- Validate input data before processing
- Return consistent error response formats
- Handle different types of errors (validation, authorization, server)
- Implement proper HTTP status codes
- Provide actionable error messages for API consumers

## Async Error Handling

- Use try-catch with async/await for readable error handling
- Handle Promise rejections explicitly
- Implement timeout handling for long-running operations
- Chain error handling through Promise catch methods when appropriate

## Error Recovery

- Implement retry mechanisms for transient failures
- Provide clear recovery actions for users
- Log errors with sufficient context for debugging
- Gracefully degrade functionality when possible
- Monitor and alert on error patterns in production
